</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this work, we propose SparseDriveV2, which introduces a scalable trajectory vocabulary representation and a scalable scoring strategy for reasoning over super-dense candidate trajectories. Extensive experiments demonstrate that SparseDriveV2 achieves SOTA performance among both scoring-based and dynamic generation methods, suggesting that with sufficiently dense vocabularies and efficient scoring mechanisms, scoring-based planning can serve as a simple yet powerful paradigm for end-to-end autonomous driving.</p>
</div>
</section>
